## 2026-10-01 superseding note — additivity results complete

This note supersedes the earlier “execution pending” and “awaiting archival” additivity notes.

The central saved-checkpoint study is complete and archived under `analysis/patching_additivity_001/`. Read `checkpoints/CP-017_patching-additivity-results.md` before changing the manuscript interpretation.

Central result:

- intervention-size dependence is **not** equivalent to channel interaction;
- `tiny_gmp` and `tiny_gap` provide exact-additivity controls in logits yet retain large intervention-size contrasts;
- singleton vector cancellation and nonlinear scoring explain part of the curve shape;
- deeper architectures, especially some BatchNorm variants, show genuine downstream non-additivity;
- the structured-versus-pixel-permuted difference is reproduced closely by the additive singleton reconstruction, so much of the spatial-bank effect is already present in singleton contribution geometry.

Key values:

- `two_concepts/tiny_gmp` probability-error (B): observed = additive = +0.83151;
- `single_shape/bn2_w16_gap` centered-logit (B): observed -0.27012 vs additive +0.34955;
- `two_concepts` structured-minus-pixel-permuted centered-logit (B), four-architecture average: observed +0.05743 vs additive +0.05710.

`paper/main.tex` now includes a compact additive-decomposition method and result section plus revised abstract/discussion/conclusion. Do not revert to wording that treats the intervention-size effect itself as evidence of nonlinear channel interaction.

No new models are required for this interpretation.


